# ApiResponseElement.java

This is Apache 2.0 licensed Open Source code from the ZAP (Zed Attack Proxy) project, so I can share it while respecting the license.

## Overview

`ApiResponseElement` extends `ApiResponse` and represents a single API response element that can hold either a string value or a nested `ApiResponse`. It provides two predefined static instances: `OK` and `FAIL`.

## The `toJSON()` Method

```java
@Override
public JSON toJSON() {
    JSONObject jo = new JSONObject();
    if (apiResponse == null) {
        jo.put(
                this.getName(),
                this.value == null
                        ? JSONNull.getInstance()
                        : JsonUtil.getJsonFriendlyString(this.value));
    } else {
        // toString() is required to prevent auto conversion of text values to JSON
        jo.put(this.getName(), apiResponse.toJSON().toString());
    }
    return jo;
}
```

**How it works:** If there's no nested `apiResponse`, it puts the name/value pair into a `JSONObject`, using `JSONNull` when the value is null. Otherwise, it embeds the nested response's JSON as a string. The inline note explains that `toString()` is used to prevent unwanted conversion of text into JSON.

## The `toXML()` Method

